    "diff": "--- /dev/null\n+++ b/content/rules/T7/rule-0291.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+{\n+  \"criteria\": {\n+    \"f02\": \"m-0291-f02\",\n+    \"f21\": \"m-0291-f21\"\n+  },\n+  \"rule_id\": \"rule-0291\",\n+  \"template\": \"T7\"\n+}\n"
  },
  "verdict": {
    "verdict": "reproduced_failure",
    "headline": "Rule 0291 for template T7 will break content-interpreter with exit code 3",
    "cause": "The new rule-0291 adds only 2 criteria fields (f02, f21) for template T7. However, the content-interpreter contract (ic-0036) requires inputs_supplied=20, and the rule-validator contract (ic-0035) requires field_count=21. When the candidate experiment runs, the interpreter encounters rule-0291 which references input slots that do not exist in its sparse 2-field criteria structure, causing exit_code=3 with the fatal error: \"rule rule-0291 read an input slot that does not exist (20 inputs supplied)\". The baseline (exit_code=0) processes 3 rules successfully with 50 events.",
    "decided_by": "deterministic_judge",
    "tested": [
      "x-ffdbc2eac6c74c97: baseline · workload default → all assertions passed",
      "x-64468c5b981e4a10: candidate · workload default → failed: interpreter_keeps_running",
      "x-2e2b7991393347e2: candidate · workload default → failed: interpreter_keeps_running",
      "x-a498394c3b2746d8: control · workload default → all assertions passed"
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "The experiments used the default workload; other workloads with different input schemas might exhibit different behavior. The rule-validator's field_count=21 check and interpreter's inputs_supplied=20 requirement were not modified to accommodate the sparse rule."
    ],
    "mitigation": {
      "text": "Add 18 more criteria fields to rule-0291 so the rule has 20+ input slots matching the interpreter's inputs_supplied=20 contract, or update the interpreter contract (ic-0036) to accept 2 inputs instead of 20.",
      "verified": false
    },
    "fix_verification": null
  },
